{
  "format": "bgsim.model",
  "language": "0.1.0",
  "name": "cube-3d-mb-soft",
  "$comment": "Plan 9.9 / DEC-M5-3 (X5.4): the multibond counterpart of cube-3d, built from the M3 spatial stdlib and run with the same controller (project:CubeLQR, same K). World -> Pivot (Spherical3D, compliant: kt = 1e+06 N/m, bt = 158 N s/m) -> Link (FixedTransform3DNeutral, the CoM r = (a/2)(1,1,1) in the corner frame) -> Body (RigidBody3D, m = 0.36 kg, J = 0.0024 kg m^2 about the CoM). Three body-axis wheels, each a RigidBody3D (m = 0.02 kg, J = (3e-4, 3e-4, 6e-4): axial Thw = 6e-4, transverse 3e-4) on a Revolute3D whose axis is the body x, y, z (mounted by FixedTransform3DNeutral), driven by an ElectricDrive (same motor as cube-3d, rotor 1e-6) through a stiff ElasticShaft (a rotor rigidly on a rate-imposing joint is W201). The wheels sit on the CoM, so the total mass is 0.42 kg and the inertia about the CoM is 3e-3 + 6e-4 = 3.6e-3 on every axis (body 2.4e-3 + own axis 6e-4 + the two other wheels' transverse 2 x 3e-4), exactly the cube-3d inertia. Measurements: PoseBody (composed pose, quaternion for the controller), Body.V (body rates), the three joint rates (wheel rates relative to the cube), TiltMeter, BodyMeasure (angular momentum about the world origin = the pivot; the vertical part summed over body and wheels is conserved).",
